{"id":"o1-04-p4","title":"Inter-process communication","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: pipes, sockets, shared memory, signals, how to choose, and Linux debugging tools. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"why-processes-need-ipc","title":"Why processes need IPC","html":"<p><strong>Processes are isolated on purpose, so to cooperate they need Inter-Process Communication (IPC): a controlled channel the kernel provides.</strong> Two families:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Message passing:</strong> data is copied through the kernel (pipes, sockets, message queues). Safe and simple.</li>\n<li><strong>Shared memory:</strong> both processes map the same physical pages. Fastest, but you must synchronise yourself.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Pick by: same machine or not, throughput, latency, need for a byte stream versus messages, who is allowed to connect, and how failure is detected.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Mechanism</th>\n<th>Same host only</th>\n<th>Direction</th>\n<th>Typical cost</th>\n<th>Good for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Pipe</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>One way</td>\n<td>Copy x2</td>\n<td>Shell pipelines, parent-child</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Named pipe (FIFO)</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>One way</td>\n<td>Copy x2</td>\n<td>Unrelated local processes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Unix domain socket</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>Two way</td>\n<td>Copy x2</td>\n<td>Local services (Docker, Postgres, Nginx to PHP-FPM)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>TCP socket</td>\n<td>No</td>\n<td>Two way</td>\n<td>Copy + network stack</td>\n<td>Anything across machines</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Shared memory</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>Both</td>\n<td>Zero copy</td>\n<td>High throughput</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Signals</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n<td>Notification only</td>\n<td>Tiny</td>\n<td>Stop, reload, kill</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 433.6 130\" width=\"433.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two safe routes between isolated processes\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 34 L331.6 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 34 L331.6 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 65 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 96 L331.6 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 96 L331.6 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Process A</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Kernel buffer</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.8\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Shared pages</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"376.6\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Process B</text></svg><figcaption>Two safe routes between isolated processes</figcaption></figure>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># What IPC objects exist on this box</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">ls</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -l</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> /proc/</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">pi</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">d</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">></span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">/fd</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">           # pipes show as pipe:[12345], sockets as socket:[...]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">ss</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -xp</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">                         # unix sockets</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">ipcs</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">                           # SysV shared memory, queues, semaphores</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">ls</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> /dev/shm</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">                    # POSIX shared memory files</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Postgres on the same host: connecting through the Unix socket <code>/var/run/postgresql/.s.PGSQL.5432</code> instead of <code>127.0.0.1:5432</code> skips the TCP/IP stack and typically shaves a few tens of microseconds per round trip, which matters for thousands of tiny queries.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Chrome uses Mojo (pipes and shared memory) between browser and renderer processes; Android Binder is a kernel IPC mechanism behind every system service call; Docker's CLI talks to the daemon over <code>/var/run/docker.sock</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Neighbours cannot walk into each other's flats: they pass notes through a letter box (messages) or agree to share one whiteboard in the hallway (shared memory).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying shared memory needs no kernel: it needs the kernel to set up the mapping, then no copies.</li>\n<li>Forgetting message passing is slower for big data because of copies and syscalls.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"pipes","title":"Pipes","html":"<p><strong>A pipe is a kernel buffer with a write end and a read end. Bytes written in come out in the same order.</strong> <code>pipe(fds)</code> returns two file descriptors. The default capacity on Linux is 64 KB (16 pages), adjustable with <code>fcntl(F_SETPIPE_SZ)</code> up to <code>/proc/sys/fs/pipe-max-size</code> (1 MB default).</p>\n<p>Semantics:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Reader blocks when empty; writer blocks when full (this is <strong>backpressure</strong>, free flow control).</li>\n<li>Writer closes and buffer empty means reader sees EOF (<code>read</code> returns 0).</li>\n<li>All readers closed means writer gets <code>SIGPIPE</code> / <code>EPIPE</code>.</li>\n<li>Writes up to <code>PIPE_BUF</code> (4096 bytes on Linux) are atomic, so concurrent writers do not interleave small lines.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>cmd1 | cmd2</code> is exactly this: the shell makes a pipe, forks twice, wires stdout of the first to the write end and stdin of the second to the read end (<code>dup2</code>), then execs.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">import</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> os</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">r, w </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> os.pipe()</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">if</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> os.fork() </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">==</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:           </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># child reads</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    os.close(w)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">    print</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(os.read(r, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">100</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">))</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    os._exit(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">os.close(r)                  </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># parent writes</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">os.write(w, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">b</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"hello\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">os.close(w)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">os.wait()</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 698 68\" width=\"698\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"ps aux | grep java | wc -l\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M248 34 L304 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 34 L304 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M394 34 L450 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M394 34 L450 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M540 34 L596 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M540 34 L596 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ps</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">pipe 1</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"349\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">grep</text><rect x=\"450\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"495\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">pipe 2</text><rect x=\"596\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"641\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">wc</text></svg><figcaption>ps aux | grep java | wc -l</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Named pipes (FIFOs):</strong> <code>mkfifo /tmp/q</code> makes a pipe with a path so unrelated processes can use it.</p>\n<p><strong>Production patterns.</strong> A deadlock: the parent writes a lot to a child's stdin and waits for it to finish, but the child's stdout pipe fills (64 KB) because the parent is not reading it; both block forever. Subprocess libraries warn about this (use <code>communicate()</code> in Python, read stdout and stderr in separate threads in Java <code>ProcessBuilder</code>). Check with <code>ls -l /proc/&#x3C;pid>/fd</code> and <code>cat /proc/&#x3C;pid>/stack</code> / <code>wchan</code> showing <code>pipe_write</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A water pipe: fill it faster than it drains and the tap has to wait.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Believing pipes are two-way. Use two pipes or a socketpair.</li>\n<li>Forgetting to close unused ends, which prevents EOF and hangs the reader.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"sockets","title":"Sockets","html":"<p><strong>A socket is a two-way communication endpoint addressed by name, used for both local and network IPC.</strong> Same API (<code>socket, bind, listen, accept, connect, send, recv</code>) for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>TCP (<code>AF_INET</code>, <code>SOCK_STREAM</code>):</strong> reliable byte stream across hosts.</li>\n<li><strong>UDP (<code>SOCK_DGRAM</code>):</strong> unreliable datagrams.</li>\n<li><strong>Unix domain (<code>AF_UNIX</code>):</strong> local only, addressed by a file path, can pass file descriptors and verify the peer's UID (<code>SO_PEERCRED</code>). Faster than loopback TCP.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Server steps:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>socket() -> bind(addr) -> listen(backlog) -> accept() -> read/write -> close</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Client:  socket() -> connect(addr) -> write/read -> close</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Each socket has kernel send and receive buffers (<code>SO_SNDBUF</code>, <code>SO_RCVBUF</code>; defaults of a few hundred KB, auto-tuned). A full send buffer blocks (or returns <code>EAGAIN</code> in non-blocking mode). The <code>listen</code> backlog (<code>somaxconn</code>, 4096 default on recent kernels) bounds queued handshakes; overflowing it drops connections: look at <code>ss -lnt</code> (Recv-Q on a listener is the accept queue) and <code>nstat -az TcpExtListenOverflows</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>$ ss -tnp state established '( sport = :8080 )' | head -3</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Recv-Q Send-Q Local Address:Port  Peer Address:Port  Process</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>0      0      10.0.1.5:8080       10.0.2.9:51022     users:((\"java\",pid=4410,fd=87))</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>$ ss -s</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Total: 1204</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>TCP:   1100 (estab 900, closed 150, orphaned 3, timewait 140)</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Handling many sockets: one thread per connection, or <strong>non-blocking with epoll</strong> (<code>epoll_create</code>, <code>epoll_ctl</code>, <code>epoll_wait</code>) so a single thread watches tens of thousands. Edge vs level triggered is a favourite detail: edge-triggered tells you only on new data, so you must read until <code>EAGAIN</code>.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 780.8 68\" width=\"780.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Server flow with epoll\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M297.2 34 L353.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M297.2 34 L353.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M449.2 34 L505.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M449.2 34 L505.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M622.8 34 L678.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M622.8 34 L678.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Clients</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"227.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Listening socket</text><rect x=\"353.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"401.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">epoll_wait</text><rect x=\"505.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"564\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Worker thread</text><rect x=\"678.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"723.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Database</text></svg><figcaption>Server flow with epoll</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Production incidents.</strong> \"Too many open files\": each socket uses a file descriptor; limit <code>ulimit -n</code> (often 1024 by default; raise to 65535+ via systemd <code>LimitNOFILE</code>). Lots of <code>TIME_WAIT</code> after rapid short connections: use keep-alive and pooling. <code>CLOSE_WAIT</code> piling up means the app forgot to <code>close()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Nginx, Redis and Node.js all rest on epoll; Envoy and HAProxy hold hundreds of thousands of sockets per box; Docker, systemd and Postgres use Unix sockets locally.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Telephone: the number is the address, you dial (connect), the other side picks up (accept), and both can talk.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Mixing TCP stream semantics with message boundaries: <code>recv</code> may return half a message; you need framing (length prefix).</li>\n<li>Raising a thread pool to fix socket exhaustion instead of the fd limit.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"shared-memory","title":"Shared memory","html":"<p><strong>Shared memory maps the same physical pages into two or more processes' address spaces. After setup no syscall or copy is needed to exchange data.</strong> It is the fastest IPC (memory speed, GB/s) but offers no synchronisation or protection: the programmers must add it.</p>\n<p>APIs:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>POSIX: <code>shm_open(\"/name\", ...)</code> creates an object under <code>/dev/shm</code> (a tmpfs), <code>ftruncate</code> sets its size, <code>mmap(MAP_SHARED)</code> maps it.</li>\n<li>SysV: <code>shmget/shmat</code> (older, see <code>ipcs -m</code>).</li>\n<li><code>mmap</code> of a regular file with <code>MAP_SHARED</code> also shares memory between processes and persists to disk.</li>\n<li>Anonymous shared mapping before <code>fork</code> shares with children.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Synchronise with process-shared mutexes or semaphores (<code>pthread_mutexattr_setpshared</code>, <code>sem_open</code>), futexes, or atomics with a lock-free ring buffer. Without it you get races and torn reads.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>Process A virtual 0x7f10... -+</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>                              +--> same physical frames</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Process B virtual 0x7e22... -+</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 476.8 130\" width=\"476.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Shared mapping, no copies\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M318.8 34 L374.8 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M318.8 34 L374.8 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 65 L158 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M318.8 96 L374.8 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M318.8 96 L374.8 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Process A</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"238.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Shared pages in RAM</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"74\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"238.4\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Semaphore</text><rect x=\"374.8\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"419.8\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Process B</text></svg><figcaption>Shared mapping, no copies</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Moving 1 GB between processes through a socket needs about 2 copies (user to kernel, kernel to user) plus syscalls, roughly 0.5 to 1 s; via shared memory it is zero copies after mapping, with only a small control message per batch. That is why trading systems, video pipelines and databases use it.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Postgres keeps <code>shared_buffers</code> (commonly 25% of RAM) in shared memory used by all backend processes. Chrome shares large buffers (images, GPU frames) between processes. Android <code>ashmem</code> / <code>memfd</code> share graphics buffers. Aeron and LMAX use shared-memory ring buffers for microsecond messaging.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure pitfalls.</strong> Leaked segments survive process death: <code>ls /dev/shm</code>, <code>ipcrm</code>. Docker defaults <code>/dev/shm</code> to 64 MB, which crashes Chrome headless and Postgres under load; use <code>--shm-size=1g</code>. Shared memory counts toward the cgroup memory limit.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A whiteboard in a shared office: instant for everyone, but two people writing at once makes a mess unless they take turns with a marker (lock).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Claiming it needs no synchronisation.</li>\n<li>Storing raw pointers in shared memory; each process maps at a different address, use offsets.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"signals","title":"Signals","html":"<p><strong>A signal is a small asynchronous notification the kernel delivers to a process: \"something happened\".</strong> It carries a number, not data. The process either runs a handler, ignores it, or takes the default action (terminate, core dump, stop, ignore).</p>\n<p>Key signals:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Signal</th>\n<th>Number</th>\n<th>Meaning</th>\n<th>Catchable</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>SIGHUP</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Terminal closed; daemons reload config</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SIGINT</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Ctrl-C</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SIGQUIT</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Quit with core/thread dump (JVM prints thread dump)</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SIGKILL</td>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>Kill immediately</td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SIGSEGV</td>\n<td>11</td>\n<td>Bad memory access</td>\n<td>Yes (rarely wise)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SIGPIPE</td>\n<td>13</td>\n<td>Write to a pipe with no reader</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SIGTERM</td>\n<td>15</td>\n<td>Polite request to exit (default for <code>kill</code>)</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SIGCHLD</td>\n<td>17</td>\n<td>Child exited</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SIGSTOP/SIGCONT</td>\n<td>19/18</td>\n<td>Pause / resume</td>\n<td>STOP no</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SIGUSR1/2</td>\n<td>10/12</td>\n<td>App-defined</td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">kill</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -TERM</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 4410</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">         # graceful stop</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">kill</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -HUP</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> $(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">cat</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> /run/nginx.pid</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)   </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># reload config without dropping connections</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">kill</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -QUIT</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> &#x3C;</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">jvm-pi</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">d</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">></span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">    # thread dump to stdout</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">kill</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -9</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 4410</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">            # last resort</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Graceful shutdown pattern in a service (Kubernetes sends SIGTERM, waits <code>terminationGracePeriodSeconds</code>, default 30 s, then SIGKILL):</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">import</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> signal, sys</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">def</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> stop</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(signum, frame):</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">    # stop accepting, finish in-flight requests, flush, then exit</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    sys.exit(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">signal.signal(signal.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">SIGTERM</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, stop)</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 497.20000000000005 130\" width=\"497.20000000000005\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Kubernetes pod shutdown\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M122.4 65 L178.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M122.4 65 L178.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M339.20000000000005 34 L395.20000000000005 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M339.20000000000005 34 L395.20000000000005 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M122.4 65 L178.4 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M122.4 65 L178.4 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M339.20000000000005 96 L395.20000000000005 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M339.20000000000005 96 L395.20000000000005 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"67.2\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">SIGTERM sent</text><rect x=\"178.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"258.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App drains requests</text><rect x=\"178.4\" y=\"74\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"258.8\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Grace period ends</text><rect x=\"395.20000000000005\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"440.20000000000005\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Exit 0</text><rect x=\"395.20000000000005\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"440.20000000000005\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">SIGKILL</text></svg><figcaption>Kubernetes pod shutdown</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Subtleties: handlers must be <strong>async-signal-safe</strong> (no <code>malloc</code>, no <code>printf</code>; usually just set a flag or write a byte to a self-pipe). Signals interrupt syscalls (<code>EINTR</code>). Standard signals do not queue (several SIGCHLD may merge into one, so loop on <code>waitpid(WNOHANG)</code>). In multithreaded programs, delivery goes to any thread that does not block it; dedicate a thread with <code>sigwait</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Production incident.</strong> Container exits with code 137 = 128 + 9: killed by SIGKILL, often the OOM killer or a grace period timeout. 143 = 128 + 15 = SIGTERM. App as shell script (<code>CMD ./start.sh</code>) does not forward SIGTERM to the Java child, so the pod is always force-killed after 30 s; use <code>exec java ...</code> in the script.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A tap on the shoulder: no message, just \"pay attention\". You may react, ignore, or (for SIGKILL) get carried out.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying you can catch SIGKILL.</li>\n<li>Doing heavy work inside a signal handler.</li>\n<li>Not knowing the difference between SIGTERM and SIGKILL in rolling deploys.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"choosing-an-ipc-mechanism","title":"Choosing an IPC mechanism","html":"<p><strong>Choose by the questions: do they share a host, how big is the data, how fast must it be, and what must survive a crash?</strong></p>\n<p>Decision guide:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Parent and child, simple stream: <strong>pipe</strong>.</li>\n<li>Local services, request/response, need peer credentials: <strong>Unix domain socket</strong> (the default sane choice).</li>\n<li>Might move to another machine later or microservices: <strong>TCP/gRPC/HTTP</strong> (network sockets; latency about 50 to 500 microseconds on LAN vs under 20 microseconds on a Unix socket).</li>\n<li>Bulk data or microsecond latency on one host: <strong>shared memory + a small signalling channel</strong>.</li>\n<li>Just \"stop / reload / ping\": <strong>signals</strong>.</li>\n<li>Durable, decoupled, many consumers: a <strong>message broker</strong> (Kafka, RabbitMQ) is IPC at system scale.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 778.8000000000001 192\" width=\"778.8000000000001\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Decision shortcut\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 96 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M290 65 L346 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M290 65 L346 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M593.2 34 L649.2 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M593.2 34 L649.2 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M290 65 L346 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M290 65 L346 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M593.2 96 L649.2 127\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M593.2 96 L649.2 127\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M102 96 L158 127\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 96 L158 127\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M290 127 L346 158\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M290 127 L346 158\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Need IPC</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"224\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Same host?</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"105\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"224\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Different hosts</text><rect x=\"346\" y=\"12\" width=\"247.20000000000002\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"469.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Big data or microsecond latency</text><rect x=\"346\" y=\"74\" width=\"247.20000000000002\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"469.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Otherwise</text><rect x=\"346\" y=\"136\" width=\"247.20000000000002\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"469.6\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">TCP or gRPC</text><rect x=\"649.2\" y=\"43\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"708\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Shared memory</text><rect x=\"649.2\" y=\"105\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"708\" y=\"131\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Unix socket</text></svg><figcaption>Decision shortcut</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Starting with sockets (even local) is a reversible, flexible choice: the same code runs across hosts. Shared memory couples processes tightly and is a harder-to-undo design. Android Binder gives each call a security identity, which is why apps use it over raw sockets.</p>\n<p><strong>Debug toolbox.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>lsof -p &#x3C;pid></code>, <code>ls -l /proc/&#x3C;pid>/fd</code>: what is open.</li>\n<li><code>ss -tnlp</code>, <code>ss -xlp</code>: listeners and Unix sockets with owners.</li>\n<li><code>strace -f -e trace=network,read,write -p &#x3C;pid></code>: what it sends.</li>\n<li><code>tcpdump -i lo port 8080</code>: loopback traffic.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Delivering a message: shout across the room (signal), pass a note (pipe), phone call (socket), shared whiteboard (shared memory), post office (broker).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Picking shared memory first because it is \"fastest\" without a measured need.</li>\n<li>Ignoring failure detection: with a pipe or socket the peer's death shows up as EOF or reset; with shared memory you must add heartbeats.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>IPC exists because processes are isolated: use message passing (copies, safe) or shared memory (zero copy, you synchronise).</li>\n<li>Pipes: one-way kernel buffer (64 KB), blocking gives backpressure; EOF when writers close; deadlock if nobody drains stdout.</li>\n<li>Sockets: two-way, TCP across hosts, Unix domain locally; know the backlog, fd limit, epoll, <code>TIME_WAIT</code>/<code>CLOSE_WAIT</code>.</li>\n<li>Shared memory (<code>shm_open</code> + <code>mmap</code>): fastest; needs mutexes or lock-free rings; mind <code>/dev/shm</code> size in Docker and leaked segments.</li>\n<li>Signals: notifications only; SIGTERM graceful, SIGKILL not catchable; exit 137 = SIGKILL, 143 = SIGTERM; handlers must be async-signal-safe.</li>\n<li>Prefer Unix sockets locally and TCP/gRPC across hosts; use shared memory only with a measured need.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}